CelloBass asset-specific licensing and attribution

This repository contains original project work, adaptations, and separately
licensed third-party source archives. Permissions depend on the asset.

O'Cello source and O'Cello-derived geometry
---------------------------------------
Author: Conor O'Kane
Project: https://o-cello.com/
License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
License URL: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
Legal text: licenses/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt

The unmodified source archive is 02_ORIGINAL_PROJECTS/O-Cello_Source.zip.
Derived assets include the exported O'Cello meshes, Blender study assemblies,
source-containing GLB/model data, and renders of the adapted instrument.
Changes made by the CelloBass project include non-string-bearing frame and
support studies, kinematic views, and mechanism prototypes. The original
evaluated musical surfaces are preserved as described in the audit reports.
Retain attribution, identify changes, and comply with the noncommercial terms.

OpenBass source archive and reference material
---------------------------------------------
Author: tbenen
Project: https://www.printables.com/model/1378247-openbass-customizable-3d-printed-multiscale-headle
License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
License URL: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Legal text: licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt

The unmodified archive is 02_ORIGINAL_PROJECTS/OpenBass_Original.zip.
The supplied project-page PDF records the license. The archive and reference
renders retain those terms. OpenBass geometry is used for source inspection
and construction reference. It is not incorporated into the CelloBass assembly.

Other CelloBass project work
---------------------------
No additional blanket license is granted for independently authored code,
documentation, and original assets by publishing this collection. Contact the
repository owner for permissions beyond those provided by an applicable
third-party license. This statement does not restrict permissions already
granted by the licenses listed above.

The seated-player storyboard and early visual references are AI-generated
concept illustrations. Prompts and provenance for the seated-player image
are retained in output/r03/source and output/r03/reports.

The original authors have not endorsed this independent prototype. Prototype
status, incomplete supports, and untested physical properties are documented
in the README and verification reports.
